{
  "$comment": [
    "Declarative matrix for the packaged-consumer test suite.",
    "`versions.latest` entries are resolved against the npm registry at prepare",
    "time and pinned into the run report, so a run is reproducible after the fact.",
    "`lts` entries are pinned by hand to the line that ships with / is recommended",
    "for the Node LTS release."
  ],
  "node": [
    {
      "id": "22",
      "version": "22",
      "channel": "lts"
    },
    {
      "id": "24",
      "version": "24",
      "channel": "current"
    }
  ],
  "packageManagers": [
    {
      "id": "npm-lts",
      "pm": "npm",
      "channel": "lts",
      "version": "10",
      "linker": "hoisted"
    },
    {
      "id": "npm-latest",
      "pm": "npm",
      "channel": "latest",
      "version": "latest",
      "linker": "hoisted"
    },
    {
      "id": "pnpm-lts",
      "pm": "pnpm",
      "channel": "lts",
      "version": "10",
      "linker": "isolated"
    },
    {
      "id": "pnpm-latest",
      "pm": "pnpm",
      "channel": "latest",
      "version": "latest",
      "linker": "isolated"
    },
    {
      "id": "yarn-lts-nm",
      "pm": "yarn",
      "channel": "lts",
      "version": "4",
      "linker": "node-modules"
    },
    {
      "id": "yarn-latest-nm",
      "pm": "yarn",
      "channel": "latest",
      "version": "latest",
      "linker": "node-modules"
    },
    {
      "id": "yarn-latest-pnp",
      "pm": "yarn",
      "channel": "latest",
      "version": "latest",
      "linker": "pnp"
    }
  ],
  "$tiers": [
    "`smoke` is the default: one Node, one version of each package manager, every",
    "playground. `full` is the whole cross product and is what you run before",
    "merging a packaging change."
  ],
  "tiers": {
    "smoke": {
      "node": ["24"],
      "packageManagers": ["npm-latest", "pnpm-latest", "yarn-latest-nm"]
    },
    "full": {
      "node": ["22", "24"],
      "packageManagers": [
        "npm-lts",
        "npm-latest",
        "pnpm-lts",
        "pnpm-latest",
        "yarn-lts-nm",
        "yarn-latest-nm",
        "yarn-latest-pnp"
      ]
    }
  },
  "$playgrounds": [
    "`stageRoot` is the directory copied into the image; `appDir` is the path",
    "inside it that gets installed and built. They differ when a playground reads",
    "sibling files (the Astro ones share a `../shared` component directory).",
    "`serve.type: none` means build-only, recorded as such in the report rather",
    "than silently skipped.",
    "`dist` is the directory the build writes, measured for the size report.",
    "`covers` lists only the packages the app depends on *directly*. Under pnpm's",
    "isolated layout a transitive dependency is deliberately not resolvable from",
    "the app root, so naming one here reports a correct install as broken."
  ],
  "playgrounds": [
    {
      "id": "duplicate-dependency",
      "dist": "dist",
      "$why": [
        "Two routes to @storyblok/preview-bridge in one app: the fixture imports",
        "it directly, and @storyblok/js reaches it through loadStoryblokBridge().",
        "`storyblok-bridge-stylesheet` is the DOM id the bridge injects and appears",
        "once per bundled copy. `offsetWidth` appears only in 2.1.6, which switched",
        "to getBoundingClientRect() sizing in 2.2.0."
      ],
      "covers": ["@storyblok/js"],
      "stageRoot": "tools/playground-matrix/fixtures/duplicate-dependency",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "fingerprints": {
        "preview-bridge copies": "storyblok-bridge-stylesheet",
        "stale 2.1.6 sizing": "offsetWidth"
      },
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectText": ["duplicate-dependency probe"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "duplicate-dependency-stress",
      "dist": "dist",
      "$why": [
        "Three shared dependencies, each reached by more than one route.",
        "@storyblok/preview-bridge: direct import, @storyblok/js, @storyblok/live-preview.",
        "@storyblok/richtext: direct import, @storyblok/js, @storyblok/vue.",
        "storyblok-js-client: direct import and the @storyblok/js api plugin.",
        "Fingerprints are string literals rather than identifiers, because",
        "identifiers get mangled and the two sides are minified differently:",
        "`storyblok-bridge-stylesheet` is the DOM id the bridge injects,",
        "`noopener noreferrer nofollow` is emitted by the richtext link renderer,",
        "and `api-ap.storyblok.com` is in the client's region table. `offsetWidth`",
        "narrows the bridge count to the stale 2.1.6 copy, which sized the overlay",
        "with offsetWidth before 2.2.0 moved to getBoundingClientRect().",
        "`covers` is empty on purpose: the externalization assertions run in the",
        "other playgrounds, and gating on them here would stop the run before the",
        "browser probe, which is the part that only means something on the base."
      ],
      "covers": [],
      "stageRoot": "tools/playground-matrix/fixtures/duplicate-dependency-stress",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "fingerprints": {
        "preview-bridge copies": "storyblok-bridge-stylesheet",
        "stale 2.1.6 sizing": "offsetWidth",
        "richtext copies": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
        "js-client copies": "api-ap.storyblok.com"
      },
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectText": ["duplicate-dependency-stress probe"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "duplicate-dependency-drift",
      "dist": "dist",
      "$why": [
        "The same dependency at two versions, because the install happened over",
        "time rather than all at once. `vendor/stale-sdk` pins",
        "@storyblok/preview-bridge at an exact 2.1.6, the way a lockfile entry",
        "written months ago would, while the app itself asks for ^2.2.0. No",
        "package manager can collapse that without an override, so both sides",
        "carry two versions in node_modules and the question is how many end up",
        "in the bundle, and whether an override can still fix it."
      ],
      "covers": [],
      "stageRoot": "tools/playground-matrix/fixtures/duplicate-dependency-drift",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "fingerprints": {
        "preview-bridge copies": "storyblok-bridge-stylesheet",
        "stale 2.1.6 sizing": "offsetWidth"
      },
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectText": ["duplicate-dependency-drift probe"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "inlined-third-party",
      "$why": [
        "`@storyblok/astro` inlines `camelcase` and `morphdom` on main: both sit",
        "inside its bundled `dist/index.js`. This fixture reaches each of them by a",
        "second route \u2014 the app imports them directly, the way an app with any",
        "transitive dependency on them already does \u2014 so the copies become countable.",
        "`covers` is empty on purpose: an externalization assertion would fail the",
        "run on main before the interesting measurement happens."
      ],
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": [],
      "stageRoot": "tools/playground-matrix/fixtures/inlined-third-party",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "fingerprints": {
        "camelcase copies": "[_.\\- ]+",
        "morphdom copies": "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
      },
      "serve": {
        "type": "node",
        "entry": "dist/server/entry.mjs",
        "port": 4321
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectText": ["inlined-third-party probe"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "js-vanilla",
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/js"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/js/playground/vanilla",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectText": ["Storyblok"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "js-vue",
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/js"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/js/playground/vue",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectSelector": ["#app"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "react-vite",
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/react", "@storyblok/richtext"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/react/playground/react",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectSelector": ["#root"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "react-next-13-app-router",
      "dist": ".next",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/react"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/react/playground/next-13-app-router",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build:demo",
      "serve": {
        "type": "script",
        "script": "start",
        "port": 3000
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "react-next-13-pages-router",
      "dist": ".next",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/react"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/react/playground/next-13-pages-router",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build:demo",
      "serve": {
        "type": "script",
        "script": "start",
        "port": 3000
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "react-next-latest",
      "dist": ".next",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/react"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/react/playground/next-latest",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "script",
        "script": "start",
        "port": 3000
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "react-next-latest-static",
      "dist": "out",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/react"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/react/playground/next-latest-static",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "out"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "astro-ssg",
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/astro"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/astro/playground",
      "appDir": "ssg",
      "build": "build:demo",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "astro-ssr",
      "dist": ".vercel/output",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/astro"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/astro/playground",
      "appDir": "ssr",
      "build": "build",
      "$serve": "Vercel adapter output; no runnable local server, so build-only.",
      "serve": {
        "type": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vue",
      "dist": "dist",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/vue"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/vue/playground/vue",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "static",
        "dir": "dist"
      },
      "smoke": {
        "expectSelector": ["#app"],
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "svelte-kit",
      "dist": ".svelte-kit/output",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/svelte"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/svelte/playground/sveltekit",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "$serve": "adapter-auto emits no runnable output off a recognised host, so build-only.",
      "serve": {
        "type": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nuxt",
      "dist": ".output",
      "covers": ["@storyblok/nuxt"],
      "stageRoot": "packages/nuxt/playground",
      "appDir": ".",
      "build": "build",
      "serve": {
        "type": "node",
        "entry": ".output/server/index.mjs",
        "port": 3000
      },
      "smoke": {
        "allowConsoleErrors": false
      }
    }
  ]
}
